{
  "meta": {
    "id": "en_b1_u20",
    "domain": "language",
    "lang": "en",
    "level": "b1",
    "unit": 20,
    "title": "Phrasal Verbs (Inseparable)",
    "title_ko": "구동사 (비분리형)",
    "focus_axis": "grammar"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "Inseparable phrasal verbs (look after, run into, get over, look into) never split — the object always comes after the whole verb, whether it's a noun or a pronoun: 'I ran into an old friend' / 'I ran into her' (never 'I ran her into').",
    "explanation_ko": "비분리형 구동사(look after, run into, get over, look into)는 절대 나뉘지 않습니다 — 목적어가 명사든 대명사든 항상 구동사 전체 뒤에 옵니다: 'I ran into an old friend' / 'I ran into her'('I ran her into'는 틀림).",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "I ran into an old classmate yesterday.",
        "ko": "저는 어제 옛 동창을 우연히 만났어요."
      },
      {
        "en": "Who's looking after your dog this week?",
        "ko": "이번 주 강아지는 누가 돌봐줘요?"
      },
      {
        "en": "It took me a while to get over the flu.",
        "ko": "독감을 회복하는 데 시간이 좀 걸렸어요."
      }
    ]
  },
  "tasks": [
